    "body": "I always found this to be a weird part of the specification... Is it really the *byte source*'s fault that the BYOB reader is trying to do a multi-byte `read(view)`, but there just aren't any more bytes? 🤔\r\n\r\nI'm wondering if we should just get rid of the \"throw _e_\" in step 4.2.3, and let the byte source tear down \"normally\" while only the reader gets the error.\r\n\r\n**Edit:** I'm moving this discussion back to https://github.com/whatwg/streams/issues/1387, since it would require quite a different PR.",
